From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:24:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] per-account economy serialization at the services and command
 boundaries

Restores, for one version-locked plugin jar, the serialization Paper used to provide
implicitly by having a single main thread - without touching, patching or instrumenting
a single byte of that plugin.

The problem. A ledger written for Paper stores the balance in a plain non-volatile field
and mutates it with a non-atomic read-modify-write spread across two calls
(setMoney(getMoney().subtract(x))). On Paper every caller runs on the one main thread, so
they serialize by construction. On Folia two players in two regions run on two threads,
the read-modify-writes interleave, and one update is silently discarded - then written
cleanly to disk by the plugin's own save executor. There is no exception, no log line and
no thread-ownership violation, because a money field is not world state: the flow never
reaches TickThread.ensureTickThread. The project's usual "ownership violations = 0" metric
is structurally blind to this failure (project-docs evidence 20260729d-t01 section 6.4).

What this does NOT do. It does not add a lock inside the plugin, make its balance field
volatile, rewrite its data model, or transform its bytecode. Those remain DEC-19 B5 and
out of scope. It does not make any refused plugin loadable either - the folia-supported
gate's refusal list (patch 0025) is a separate mechanism and is untouched here.

Where it hooks instead - two boundaries the core already owns:

1. Services boundary. CraftServer's ServicesManager is a core object, and a plugin
   registers its economy provider into it (for EssentialsX: Essentials.java:205 registers
   VaultEconomyProvider under net.milkbowl.vault.economy.Economy). Every Vault consumer on
   the server - shop plugins, reward plugins, server tweaks - resolves that one object, so
   wrapping it once covers all of them. LophinyaServicesManager subclasses
   SimpleServicesManager and hands each registration to
   LophinyaEconomySerialization.wrapServiceProvider, which returns a java.lang.reflect.Proxy
   holding a per-account lock for the duration of each call. Different accounts still run
   fully in parallel; only same-account calls serialize.

2. Legacy command boundary. The plugin's own economy commands (/pay, /eco, /sell,
   /balance) never go through Vault - they call the plugin's internal API, which the core
   cannot see. BukkitCommandNode:83 is the single point through which every plugin.yml
   command is executed, so a guarded plugin's economy commands run there under a coarse
   exclusive lock that also excludes every service-boundary call. The lock is coarse
   because at that point the core knows which plugin owns the command but not which
   accounts the body will touch - /pay names its target only inside the plugin's own
   argument parsing, and hardcoding a third-party command's argument format into the core
   is exactly the scattered plugin-specific hardcoding AGENTS.md line 12 forbids. These are
   human-typed commands at single-digit frequency; the high-frequency path is the service
   boundary, which stays per-account.

Lock order and liveness. The only order ever taken is coarse -> account, and account locks
are acquired in sorted key order when a call names more than one account. Nothing is held
across a scheduler hand-off, a chunk load or a future: every critical section is a
straight-line call into the plugin and back, so a region thread blocked on one of these is
always waiting on a section that is itself making progress. ReentrantReadWriteLock permits
taking the read lock while already holding the write lock, so a command that internally
reaches back through the service boundary downgrades rather than self-deadlocking.

Fail-open, unlike patch 0026. The scheduler dispatch registry fails closed (an unreadable
field means "do not dispatch"). This one fails open: if the rule lookup, the jar hash or
the proxy construction fails, the original provider is registered unwrapped and the server
behaves exactly as it does today. The asymmetry is deliberate - this patch never grants a
plugin new reach, it only narrows concurrency for a plugin that is already running, so a
failure here can lose the added protection but can never create a new code path.

Rule table. Keyed by exact jar SHA-256, same versioning discipline as patch 0026: a plugin
update needs a fresh entry with fresh research, it never inherits the previous version's
guard. The only entry is EssentialsX 2.22.1-dev+12-776f709, the artifact installed on s01.
balancetop is deliberately not guarded: it is read-only and already scans the whole
userdata set off-thread, so putting it under the exclusive lock would stall every region
thread for a full scan to protect a value that is advisory by design.

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.economySerialization=true - defaults to OFF. With the switch
off, LophinyaServicesManager registers every provider byte-for-byte as SimpleServicesManager
did and the command hook is a single boolean test.

Research and measurements: project-docs evidence 20260729d-t01-essentialsx-callsite-analysis.md
and 20260730b-essentialsx-economy-serialization.md.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/command/brigadier/bukkit/BukkitCommandNode.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/command/brigadier/bukkit/BukkitCommandNode.java
index 5c52b1563d20d7e977a5bb958c18b19dec5c365a..eedaa4bf1f63c59e1cd88141806703d56c96f1ed 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/command/brigadier/bukkit/BukkitCommandNode.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/command/brigadier/bukkit/BukkitCommandNode.java
@@ -80,6 +80,20 @@ public class BukkitCommandNode extends LiteralCommandNode<CommandSourceStack> {
             String[] args = org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils.split(content, ' '); // fix adjacent spaces (from console/plugins) causing empty array elements
 
             // Note: we don't return the result of target.execute as thats success / failure, we return handled (true) or not handled (false)
+            // Lophinya start - economy serialization: this is the single choke point through which
+            // every legacy (plugin.yml) Bukkit command is executed, so it is where the core can put
+            // a guarded plugin's own economy commands under the same lock as its Vault provider.
+            // See fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaEconomySerialization; no-op when the switch is off.
+            if (fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaEconomySerialization.isGuardedCommand(this.command)) {
+                fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaEconomySerialization.beginExclusive();
+                try {
+                    this.command.execute(sender, this.literal, Arrays.copyOfRange(args, 1, args.length));
+                } finally {
+                    fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaEconomySerialization.endExclusive();
+                }
+                return 1;
+            }
+            // Lophinya end - economy serialization
             this.command.execute(sender, this.literal, Arrays.copyOfRange(args, 1, args.length));
 
             // return true as command was handled
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
index e8359235c5fa0681c2d0d12cf66d6abbc0fe4d97..88d03cecae2861c263dfe9334af338d08db98b1c 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftServer.java
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@ public final class CraftServer implements Server {
     private final String serverVersion;
     private final String bukkitVersion = Versioning.getBukkitVersion();
     private final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger("Minecraft");
-    private final ServicesManager servicesManager = new SimpleServicesManager();
+    private final ServicesManager servicesManager = new fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaServicesManager(); // Lophinya - economy serialization: wrap version-locked economy providers on register (subclass is a no-op when the kill switch is off)
     private final CraftScheduler scheduler = new CraftScheduler();
     private final CraftCommandMap commandMap; // Paper - Move down
     private final SimpleHelpMap helpMap = new SimpleHelpMap(this);
